    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Chain integrity by month",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "dcms-postgres"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "dcms-postgres"
          },
          "rawSql": "\nSELECT\n    tenant_slug,\n    period,\n    first_seq,\n    last_seq,\n    row_count,\n    sealed_at,\n    rows_dropped\nFROM obs.v_audit_integrity\nORDER BY period DESC, tenant_slug\nLIMIT 200\n",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "description": "An anchor is what lets a month whose rows were dropped by retention still be shown to have been intact. A month with no sealed_at is either the current one or one that refused to seal — and a segment refuses to seal precisely when its chain does not verify, so retention leaves it alone. Look for 'Refusing to seal audit segment' at Critical.",
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true,
        "footer": {
          "show": false,
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "countRows": false,
          "fields": ""
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Audit anchors and critical audit lines",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "dcms-loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "dcms-loki"
          },
          "expr": "{service=~\"admin-api|identity|content-api|ai-gateway|media-worker|site-host\"} |~ \"AUDIT ANCHOR|Refusing to seal|Audit gap\"",
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "description": "These lines are logged at Critical as a routing instruction, not because they are errors. The runbook is explicit that an anchor existing only in the database it attests to is not an off-box anchor — this panel, and the 90-day Loki retention behind it, is what makes it one.",
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      }
    }
  ]
